surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cintorino</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005a</year><article-title>Improvement in hepatic parenchymal transection for living-related liver donor</article-title><source>Transplant Proc</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>2589</fpage><lpage>91</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16182753</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b5-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gruttadauria</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Vasta</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Mandala</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005b</year><article-title>Basiliximab in a triple drug regimen with tacrolimus and steroids in liver transplantation</article-title><source>Transplantation Proceedings</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>2611</fpage><lpage>3205</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16182762</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b6-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heffron</surname><given-names>TG</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruttadauria</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Campi</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Surgical innovations in pediatric liver transplantation reduced-size, split, and living-related transplantation</article-title><source>Prob Gen Surg</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>11</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kahan</surname><given-names>BD</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajagopalan</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Reduction of the occurrence of acute cellular rejection among renal allograft recipients treated with basiliximab, a chimeric anti-interleukin-2-receptor monoclonal antibody</article-title><source>Transplantation</source><volume>67</volume><fpage>276</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10075594</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marcos</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Right lobe living donor liver transplantation a review</article-title><source>Liver Transpl</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10648573</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marino</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name><name><surname>Doria</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>VL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Efficacy and safety of basiliximab with a tacrolimus-based regimen in liver transplant recipients</article-title><source>Transplantation</source><volume>78</volume><fpage>886</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15385809</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moser</surname><given-names>MAJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Options for induction immunosuppression in liver transplant recipients</article-title><source>Drugs</source><volume>62</volume><fpage>995</fpage><lpage>1011</lpage><issue>17</issue><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11985487</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nashan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Moore</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Amlot</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Randomised trial of basiliximab versus placebo for control of acute cellular rejection in renal allograft recipients</article-title><source>Lancet</source><volume>350</volume><fpage>1193</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9652559</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Otte</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>History of pediatric liver transplantation. Where are we coming from? Where do we stand</article-title><source>Pediatric Transplant</source><volume>6</volume><fpage>378</fpage><lpage>87</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ponticelli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Yussim</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cambi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>A randomized, double-blind trial of basiliximab immunoprophylaxis plus triple therapy in kidney transplant recipients</article-title><source>Transplantation</source><volume>72</volume><fpage>1261</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11602853</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ringe</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Moritz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Zeldin</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>What is the best immunosuppression in living donor liver transplantation</article-title><source>Transplant Proc</source><volume>37</volume><fpage>2169</fpage><lpage>71</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15964369</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-btt-1-69"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singh</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Paterson</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Gayowski</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Cytomegalovirus antigenemia directed pre-emptive prophylaxis with oral versus I.V. ganciclovir for the prevention of cytomegalovirus disease in liver transplant recipients a randomized, controlled trial</article-title><source>Transplantation</source><volume>70</volume><fpage>717</fpage><lpage>22</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11003347</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="f1-btt-1-69" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Actuarial survival curve of the patients and grafts in the 60 living-related liver transplants performed (3 years).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="btt-1-69f1"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-btt-1-69" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Demographic characteristics of 60 living donors and recipients</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">Donor<hr/></th><th colspan="2" align="left" rowspan="1">Recipient<hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Characteristics</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">n</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mean &#x000b1; SD or percent</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">n</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mean &#x000b1; SD or percent</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Age</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">32.26 &#x